<title>POLAND: Polish broad money rises 0.9 pct in Nov 1-10 - NBP.</title>
<headline>Polish broad money rises 0.9 pct in Nov 1-10 - NBP.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's broad money rose by 1.11 billion zlotys, or 0.9 percent, in November 1-10 to 127.15 billion after a 2.2 percent rise in the whole of October, preliminary central bank figures showed.</p>
<p> BROAD POLISH MONEY		  NOV 1-10 96  OCT  NOV 1-10 95</p>
<p>  month/month change (pct)		0.9	2.2	 1.3</p>
<p>  Money in bln zlotys		   127.15   126.04     98.71</p>
<p>  Foreign currency (in bln PLN)	22.61    22.51     20.85</p>
<p>  National currency		     104.53   103.53     77.86</p>
<p>  Cash in circulation		    23.64    23.51     18.91</p>
<p>  Lending to non-financial sector    74.10    73.41     53.99</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
